    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are looking for a high-ceiling performance today, spearheaded by **Gunnar Henderson** (79.74), who remains our primary catalyst against Kremer. His favorable platoon edge and leadoff positioning create an elite scoring environment. We are also leaning heavily into our outfield depth against Noah Cameron; both **Kyle Tucker** (67.10) and **Andy Pages** (63.45) benefit significantly from an aggressive wind-out factor, which bolsters their power upside. Despite facing a challenging arm in Freddy Peralta, **Jacob Wilson** (65.32) holds strong as our SS play, buoyed by a prime #3 spot in the order that maximizes his scoring potential despite the elevated xERA of his opponent.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the final OF slot. While **Wade Meckler** (42.35) remains active, he was the closest to hitting the bench; his platoon disadvantage against the lefty MacKenzie Gore dragged down his projection, and he only narrowly survived the cut over our other rotational depth pieces. Conversely, **Drake Baldwin** (54.36) remains a viable, albeit marginal, start at C1, though managers must monitor the 37% rain risk in his matchup. We continue to manage the health of our core; **Luis Robert Jr.** remains inactive, and we are still navigating the absence of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Nasim Nunez**, whose unavailability limits our flexibility in the utility and middle infield spots. \n\nWe are keeping a close eye on **Liam Hicks** (52.88) and **Luis Lara** (42.99), as both are currently in \"lineup pending\" status. Should the confirmed orders deviate significantly from our projections, their efficiency scores could fluctuate. **Jackson Merrill** (50.36) is a high-risk, high-reward play today; while he is currently slotted for a start, he faces the toughest opposing arm of our day in the 2.82 xERA of Logan Henderson. The Waves' path to winning the SB category today hinges on the efficiency of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Andy Pages**; if they can exploit their respective matchups, we should see the necessary movement in the standings to keep pace in this tight 5x5 race.",
